+While `NoopVectorDBStorage` is active, `bypass` always works and `naive` never
+does (it has no graph entry point). `local`, `global`, `hybrid`, and `mix` need
+either rebuilt vector indexes (`lightrag-rebuild-vdb`) or the graph-only lookup
+below; by default they fail closed with an error that names both options.
+
+#### Graph-only querying
+
+`kg_entity_lookup_method="LABEL"` (env `KG_ENTITY_LOOKUP_METHOD=LABEL`) is the
+explicit opt-in for querying a workspace loaded with `NoopVectorDBStorage`. It
+replaces the entity and relationship vector lookups, never catches the vector
+storage's error, and leaves the default `VECTOR` path byte-for-byte unchanged,
+answer-cache hashes included.
+
+```python
+rag = LightRAG(
+    working_dir=WORKING_DIR,
+    llm_model_func=llm_model_func,
+    embedding_func=None,
+    vector_storage="NoopVectorDBStorage",
+    kg_entity_lookup_method="LABEL",
+)
+```
+
+How a query is resolved under `LABEL`:
+
+- The LLM's low-level and high-level keywords are split on commas and each term
+  is passed to `BaseGraphStorage.search_labels` (case-insensitive fuzzy match on
+  every backend). Only when a multi-word term matches nothing are its tokens of
+  three or more characters searched, so `Ikhlass Boukrouh` still reaches a node
+  stored as `Boukrouh, Ikhlass`. Hits are merged round-robin across terms,
+  deduplicated, and capped at `top_k`.
+- Matched entities are expanded exactly as in `VECTOR` mode: node payloads,
+  degree as `rank`, and their edges sorted by rank and weight. High-level
+  keywords have no relation-name index, so `global` resolves them to entities
+  and takes those entities' edges; thematic keywords that are not entity names
+  yield an explicit empty result.
+- KG chunk selection uses `WEIGHT`, and `mix` skips vector chunks when the
+  chunks storage does not persist vectors (both logged). Keywords are never
+  embedded, so no embedding function is needed.
+
+Precision depends on the LLM keywords matching entity names: this is a name
+lookup, not a semantic one, and `search_labels` is a full scan on
+`NetworkXStorage`. Set the knob before `initialize_storages()`; it is read from
+the storage configuration snapshot.
 
 If the semantic-vector (`V`) chunker is selected while `embedding_func=None`,
 it logs a warning and falls back to recursive-character chunking. Configure an
